 "notes": "CardDemo's delete-user screen (transaction CU03, program COUSR03C): entered from the user list with a selected user it reads the user FOR UPDATE and shows it; ENTER looks a user up, PF5 reads it FOR UPDATE and DELETEs it -- even when the read found nothing, so the DELETE then has no record held (INVREQ, 'Unable to Update User...'); PF3 / PF12 return, PF4 clears. Each scenario's USRSEC file is compared after the task. usrsec.txt is CardDemo's own DUSRSECJ in-stream data. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own."
